'' TKO0820 -- fbc's 20: a UDT compared with a number or an enum takes a number from its casts,
'' a numeric one or a BYREF z/wstring. With casts to string or any ptr alone, every comparison
'' below is error 20 on fbc-modern 1.20 (2026-11-13); tiko let them through and the build
'' stopped on TKO0994 ("this N_IF was not compiled"). sys/win/com's CInt96 with its
'' 'operator =' private was the case: 'if n = 12345'. A numeric cast beside a string one
'' compares, and a string cast compares with a string. See proccheck.tiko, CheckUdtCompare_.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -c tests/diagnostics/src/udt-number-compare.bas -o tests/diagnostics/src/udt-number-compare.o
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: udt-number-compare.bas(20,7): error TKO0820: no operator '=' takes these operand types
'' EXPECT-OUT: udt-number-compare.bas(21,6): error TKO0820: no operator '<>' takes these operand types
'' EXPECT-OUT: udt-number-compare.bas(22,7): error TKO0820: no operator '<' takes these operand types
'' EXPECT-OUT: udt-number-compare.bas(23,7): error TKO0820: no operator '>=' takes these operand types
'' EXPECT-OUT: udt-number-compare.bas(24,7): error TKO0820: no operator '=' takes these operand types
'' EXPECT-OUT: udt-number-compare.bas(25,7): error TKO0820: no operator '=' takes these operand types
'' EXPECT-NOT: udt-number-compare.bas(26,
'' EXPECT-NOT: udt-number-compare.bas(27,
'' EXPECT-NOT: udt-number-compare.bas(28,
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0994
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 6
